meta {
  name: Create Daily Log - Sleep Pattern
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/{{houseId}}/young-persons/{{youngPersonId}}/daily-logs
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  chronology_id: 12
  activity_action: YP went to bed at 22:00. Settled quickly after bedtime routine. No disturbances during night. Woke naturally at 07:00. Total sleep: 9 hours. Sleep quality: Good. YP reports feeling refreshed.
  wake_up_time: 07:00
  wake_up_notes: Woke naturally without alarm. In good mood. Ready for breakfast.
  mood[0]: Refreshed
  mood[1]: Happy
  breakfast: Pancakes and fruit
  ~attachments[0]: @file(/path/to/sleep_chart.pdf)
}

docs {
  # Create Daily Log - Sleep Pattern
  
  Monitor and record young person's sleep patterns and quality.
  
  ## Required Fields
  - `chronology_id` (integer): Must be 12 (Sleep Pattern)
  
  **Note:** `date`, `log_date_time`, and `day_part` are automatically set by the server.
  - `activity_action` (string): Detailed sleep information
  
  ## Essential Sleep Information
  
  ### Bedtime Routine
  - Time went to bed
  - Bedtime routine activities
  - How quickly settled
  - Any resistance or issues
  
  ### Sleep Duration
  - Time fell asleep (approximate)
  - Time woke up
  - Total hours of sleep
  - Naps during day
  
  ### Sleep Quality
  - Disturbances during night
  - Number of wake-ups
  - Reasons for waking
  - How easily went back to sleep
  
  ### Morning Wake-Up
  - How woke up (naturally/alarm/staff)
  - Mood upon waking
  - Energy level
  - Readiness for day
  
  ## Recommended Fields
  - `wake_up_time` (time): Exact wake-up time (HH:MM)
  - `wake_up_notes` (string): Morning observations
  - `day_part` (string): Auto-detected (usually "Morning")
  - `mood` (array): Mood upon waking
  - `breakfast` (string): First meal
  - `attachments` (files): Sleep charts, tracking sheets
  
  ## Example Entries
  
  ### Good Sleep Pattern
  ```
  Bedtime: 21:30 - Followed normal routine (shower, reading, lights out)
  Settled: Within 15 minutes
  Night: Uninterrupted sleep, no wake-ups
  Wake time: 07:00 (natural, no alarm needed)
  Duration: 9.5 hours
  Quality: Excellent
  Morning mood: Energetic and positive
  Breakfast: Full breakfast eaten
  ```
  
  ### Disturbed Sleep
  ```
  Bedtime: 21:00 - YP appeared anxious
  Settled: Took 45 minutes, needed reassurance
  Night: Woke at 01:30 (bad dream), staff provided comfort
  Returned to sleep: 02:00
  Wake time: 07:30 (appeared tired)
  Duration: 8 hours (interrupted)
  Quality: Fair - disrupted by nightmare
  Morning mood: Tired, slightly withdrawn
  Actions: Extra support during day, relaxation before next bedtime
  ```
  
  ### Late Night / Difficulty Settling
  ```
  Bedtime routine started: 21:00
  In bed: 21:30
  Settled: After multiple check-ins, finally asleep ~23:00
  Issues: YP restless, worried about school test
  Interventions: Calm conversation, breathing exercises, 
  reassurance about test preparation
  Wake time: 08:00 (required waking)
  Duration: ~9 hours but delayed onset
  Quality: Good once asleep
  Morning: Sluggish but improved after breakfast
  Follow-up: Review stress management strategies
  ```
  
  ### Daytime Sleep
  ```
  Afternoon nap: 14:00-15:30 (90 minutes)
  Reason: YP appeared very tired after lunch
  Quality: Deep sleep, peaceful
  Impact: More alert and engaged in afternoon activities
  Night sleep: As usual, 22:00-07:00
  Note: May need to monitor if daytime naps become pattern
  ```
  
  ## Sleep Issues to Monitor
  - Difficulty falling asleep (>30 mins)
  - Frequent night waking (>2 times)
  - Early morning waking
  - Excessive daytime sleepiness
  - Irregular sleep schedule
  - Sleep less than 8-10 hours (age-dependent)
  - Nightmares or night terrors
  - Sleep walking or talking
  
  ## Best Practices
  - Document consistently every morning
  - Note patterns over time
  - Include environmental factors (noise, temperature)
  - Record any sleep aids used (medication, white noise, etc.)
  - Link to mood and behaviour patterns
  - Share concerns with healthcare team
  
  ## Response (201 Created)
  Returns the created sleep pattern log for monitoring and analysis.
}
